{% set T = inhoud.talen[lang] %}
<p class="intro intro--initiaal">Being a Christian does not begin with what we do, but with God who calls. It is a life of daily conversion: turning away from sin and returning to Him, again and again. You don’t learn that all at once. This page helps you on your way.</p>

<h2 id="bible">Start with the Bible</h2>
<p>God speaks through His Word. Read a little every day, preferably at a fixed time. The Gospel of John is a good place to begin. Read slowly and ask God to help you understand.</p>
<p><a href="/en/word/bible/">Bibles and Bible websites</a></p>

<h2 id="church">Find a church</h2>
<p>Faith is not lived alone. Look for a Bible-faithful congregation near you, where God’s Word is preached faithfully. There you will meet others walking the same road. Don’t hesitate to simply walk in.</p>
<p><a href="/en/word/preached/">Church services and a church near you</a></p>

<h2 id="pray">Learn to pray</h2>
<p>Prayer is speaking with God. You don’t need fine words. The Lord Jesus taught His disciples the Lord’s Prayer (Matthew 6:9–13); it is a good example to start with.</p>

<h2 id="questions">Ask your questions</h2>
<p>Doubts and questions are part of faith. Take them to your minister, an elder or someone you trust. You can also ask your question online.</p>
<p><a href="/en/going-deeper/">Answers to questions of faith</a></p>

